    "shortDesc": "Sedatv/hyp/anxiolytc abuse with withdrawal delirium",
    "longDesc": "Sedative, hypnotic or anxiolytic abuse with withdrawal delirium",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a condition where someone is abusing sedatives, sleeping pills, or anti-anxiety medications and is experiencing withdrawal delirium—a serious mental state that occurs when they suddenly stop or reduce use of these drugs. Withdrawal delirium involves confusion, hallucinations, agitation, and potentially dangerous physical symptoms like rapid heart rate or seizures, making it a medical emergency that requires immediate treatment.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, emergency medicine doctors, and hospital-based detoxification programs use this code when treating patients in acute withdrawal from sedative-type substances. It commonly appears in hospital and emergency department records rather than on routine patient EOBs, as it typically indicates inpatient or urgent care treatment.",
