    "shortDesc": "Sedatv/hyp/anxiolytc dependence w withdrawal delirium",
    "longDesc": "Sedative, hypnotic or anxiolytic dependence with withdrawal delirium",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that a person has become physically dependent on sedative, hypnotic, or anti-anxiety medications (such as benzodiazepines or sleeping pills) and is currently experiencing withdrawal delirium—a serious and potentially dangerous mental state that can occur when stopping these drugs. Withdrawal delirium involves confusion, hallucinations, rapid heartbeat, and severe agitation that happens as the body reacts to the sudden absence of the medication it had become dependent on. This is a medical emergency requiring careful monitoring and treatment.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, addiction medicine specialists, emergency medicine doctors, and hospital-based medical teams use this code when treating patients in acute withdrawal from sedatives or anti-anxiety medications. This code typically appears on EOB statements for patients admitted to emergency departments or inpatient psychiatric/detoxification facilities, and may also be documented during intensive outpatient addiction treatment programs.",
