    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that someone has used cocaine and is currently experiencing intoxication from it, but without serious complications like seizures, severe confusion, or dangerous vital sign changes. Cocaine intoxication can cause increased heart rate, elevated blood pressure, agitation, anxiety, or dilated pupils—essentially, the acute effects of the drug on the body and mind. This coding category is used when the person's cocaine use is documented but the specific pattern (occasional vs. dependent) isn't clarified in the medical record.",
