    "plainEnglish": "This code means you have a dependence on stimulant drugs other than cocaine or methamphetamine—such as prescription stimulants (like Adderall or Ritalin), caffeine pills, or other similar substances—and your condition is not currently complicated by withdrawal symptoms, overdose, or other serious medical or psychiatric problems. Dependence means your body and mind have adapted to regularly using the drug, and you may experience cravings or difficulty stopping use on your own.",
    "whoUses": "This code is commonly used by addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, primary care doctors, and substance abuse counselors in outpatient or inpatient treatment settings. It typically appears on EOB statements when a patient is being treated for stimulant use disorder without acute complications, and is one of the more frequently seen substance use diagnoses in behavioral health billing.",
