    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that you have a history of dependence on stimulant drugs (such as cocaine, methamphetamine, or prescription stimulants like Adderall), but you are currently in remission—meaning you're not actively using or meeting the criteria for active addiction right now. Being in remission doesn't mean the dependence is cured, but rather that you've achieved a period of recovery and are managing your condition successfully, often through treatment, support, or abstinence.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, and substance abuse counselors use this code when documenting a patient's recovery status during ongoing care, follow-up visits, or when transitioning patients to maintenance treatment. It commonly appears on EOB statements when patients attend addiction treatment programs, psychiatric appointments related to substance use history, or recovery-focused therapy sessions.",
