    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a situation where someone has become dependent on hallucinogenic drugs (like LSD, psilocybin mushrooms, or mescaline) and is also experiencing a mood disorder directly caused by using those drugs. Dependence means the person has developed a pattern of use where they feel they need the drug to function, may use more over time, and struggle to cut back. The mood disorder could involve depression, anxiety, or mood swings that result from the hallucinogen use itself, rather than being a separate condition.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, and substance use disorder treatment providers use this code when treating patients with hallucinogen dependence complicated by mood symptoms. It commonly appears in inpatient or outpatient addiction treatment settings and may show on EOB statements for those receiving mental health or addiction services, though insurance coverage for addiction treatment varies significantly by plan.",
