    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means you have developed a physical or psychological dependence on hallucinogenic drugs (like LSD, psilocybin mushrooms, or similar substances) and are experiencing additional health problems caused by that drug use. Dependence means your body or mind has adapted to the drug, so you need it to feel normal or to avoid withdrawal symptoms, and you're also dealing with other complications from the hallucinogens themselves—which could include mood changes, confusion, or other mental health effects that persist even when you're not using the drug.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, and substance use disorder treatment providers use this code when treating patients with hallucinogen dependence. It may appear on EOB statements if a patient receives treatment at a mental health clinic, rehabilitation facility, or hospital for substance use disorder, though the code is more commonly seen in clinical records and treatment summaries than on typical outpatient insurance claims.",
