    "longDesc": "Nicotine dependence, unspecified, uncomplicated",
    "plainEnglish": "This code means you have a physical and/or psychological addiction to nicotine, but your doctor hasn't specified which form (cigarettes, vaping, chewing tobacco, etc.) or identified any serious complications from your use. Nicotine dependence develops when your body becomes accustomed to nicotine and experiences cravings or withdrawal symptoms when you try to quit or go without it.",
    "whoUses": "Primary care doctors, pulmonologists, cardiologists, addiction medicine specialists, and mental health providers use this code when treating patients who smoke or use nicotine products and want to document the addiction for counseling, medication (like nicotine patches or prescription cessation drugs), or monitoring. It commonly appears on EOB statements when patients discuss tobacco use during office visits or participate in smoking cessation programs.",
