    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that you have been diagnosed with nicotine dependence (addiction to cigarettes, vaping, chewing tobacco, or other nicotine products), but you are currently in remission—meaning you've stopped using nicotine and are not actively smoking or using these products. Your doctor is documenting that while you have a history of nicotine addiction, you're no longer dependent on it at this time, though the condition remains part of your medical record because people with nicotine dependence are at higher risk of relapse.",
    "whoUses": "This code is commonly used by primary care physicians, addiction medicine specialists, and pulmonologists to track patients who have successfully quit smoking or nicotine use. It frequently appears on patient EOB statements when they visit their doctor after quitting and may be relevant for insurance purposes, as some plans offer smoking cessation support or track quit status for premium calculations.",
