    "longDesc": "Inhalant use, unspecified, uncomplicated",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that you are using inhalant substances (like glue, spray paint, or other volatile chemicals) without specifying which inhalant or whether you have developed dependence or addiction. Inhalants are chemicals that people breathe in to get high, and chronic use can damage your brain, heart, liver, and kidneys. This code simply documents the use itself without noting specific medical complications that may have resulted.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, primary care doctors, and emergency medicine physicians use this code when documenting substance use during screening, counseling, or treatment visits. It commonly appears on EOB statements when patients receive care for substance use evaluation or treatment programs, though it may also be used during routine medical visits where inhalant use is disclosed.",
