    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse, uncomplicated",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes substance abuse involving drugs or inhalants other than alcohol, opioids, cannabis, or stimulants—such as hallucinogens, club drugs, or prescription medications used non-medically. The 'uncomplicated' part means the person is abusing these substances but doesn't currently have serious withdrawal symptoms, overdose, or major mental health complications from the use. You might see this code if you've sought treatment for problematic use of substances that don't fit into the more common abuse categories.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, substance abuse counselors, and primary care physicians use this code when documenting and billing for treatment of non-standard drug abuse. It commonly appears on EOBs for patients receiving counseling, detoxification programs, or medication-assisted treatment for 'other' psychoactive substance misuse.",
