    "shortDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse, in remission",
    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse, in remission",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that you have a history of abusing drugs or other psychoactive substances (anything beyond alcohol, opioids, stimulants, or other specifically classified drugs), but you are currently in remission—meaning you are not actively using or abusing these substances right now. Remission means you've stopped the problematic use pattern, either through treatment, recovery, or sustained abstinence, though the code acknowledges your past struggle with substance abuse.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, primary care physicians, and substance abuse counselors use this code during outpatient follow-up visits and ongoing recovery monitoring. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients in recovery programs, mental health treatment, or routine check-ups where substance abuse history is being tracked for continued care coordination.",
