    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a situation where someone is misusing drugs or other mind-altering substances (like inhalants, prescription medications, or other drugs not specifically classified as alcohol, opioids, or stimulants) and is currently experiencing intoxication from that use. The person is intoxicated but doesn't have serious complications like seizures, delirium, or dangerous vital sign changes at this moment. Intoxication means the substance is actively affecting their brain and body, causing impaired judgment, coordination problems, or altered mental states.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, emergency room physicians, and substance abuse treatment providers use this code when evaluating or treating patients with documented misuse of miscellaneous psychoactive substances. It commonly appears in clinical settings like detoxification units, psychiatric hospitals, and addiction treatment centers, and may show up on EOB statements when insurance covers evaluation or treatment for substance use disorders.",
