    "shortDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse with withdrawal, uncomp",
    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse with withdrawal, uncomplicated",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes someone who is struggling with abuse of drugs or chemicals other than alcohol, cocaine, opioids, or common substances (like inhalants or hallucinogens), and they are experiencing withdrawal symptoms when they stop using. Withdrawal means their body has become physically dependent, so when they're not using the substance, they feel uncomfortable physical or emotional symptoms—such as shaking, sweating, anxiety, or irritability—but these symptoms are manageable and not causing serious complications.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, substance abuse counselors, and primary care doctors use this code when treating patients in rehabilitation or detoxification programs. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients seeking inpatient or outpatient treatment for polysubstance abuse or use of less-commonly-abused drugs.",
