    "shortDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse with withdrawal delirium",
    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance abuse with withdrawal delirium",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a serious condition where someone is abusing drugs or other psychoactive substances (not including alcohol, opioids, stimulants, or other specifically classified drugs) and is experiencing withdrawal delirium—a dangerous state of confusion, hallucinations, and agitation that occurs when they suddenly stop or reduce their use. Withdrawal delirium is a medical emergency that can include rapid heart rate, seizures, severe anxiety, and disorientation, requiring immediate treatment to prevent serious complications.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, emergency medicine physicians, and hospitalists use this code when treating patients in acute withdrawal from miscellaneous drugs like inhalants, hallucinogens, or other unspecified psychoactive substances. It commonly appears on EOB statements for emergency department visits, inpatient psychiatric or medical hospital stays, and addiction treatment admissions where patients require medical stabilization during withdrawal.",
