    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance dependence with intoxication, uncomplicated",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis means you have developed a physical and/or psychological dependence on a psychoactive substance (such as inhalants, sedatives not otherwise classified, or other drugs) and you are currently experiencing intoxication from that substance without serious complications like seizures or altered mental state. Intoxication refers to the immediate effects of the drug in your system—such as impaired judgment, coordination problems, or emotional changes—while dependence means your body or mind has become reliant on the substance.",
