    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance dependence with withdrawal, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "This code means you have a dependency on drugs or substances (not including alcohol, opioids, cannabis, stimulants, hallucinogens, or inhalants) and are experiencing withdrawal symptoms when you stop or reduce use. Withdrawal can include physical symptoms like tremors, sweating, nausea, and anxiety, as well as psychological symptoms like irritability or depression. The 'unspecified' part indicates that the exact withdrawal symptoms aren't detailed in your medical record.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, primary care doctors, and substance abuse counselors use this code when treating patients in detoxification or recovery programs. It commonly appears on EOBs for inpatient or outpatient addiction treatment visits, particularly when the specific substance causing withdrawal cannot be precisely identified or documented.",
    "billable": true,
