    "rawCode": "F1990",
    "shortDesc": "Other psychoactive substance use, unspecified, uncomplicated",
    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance use, unspecified, uncomplicated",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that you have been using psychoactive substances (drugs or chemicals that affect mood, perception, or behavior) in a way that is not otherwise specified or detailed in your medical record. The 'uncomplicated' part means that at this point, there are no documented serious health consequences, withdrawal symptoms, or mental health complications directly linked to this substance use. This is a general category your doctor might use when the specific substance isn't clearly documented or when substance use is identified but hasn't yet caused documented medical or psychiatric problems.",
    "whoUses": "This code is used by psychiatrists, addiction medicine specialists, primary care physicians, and emergency department doctors when screening or documenting substance use. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients in addiction treatment programs, mental health evaluations, or routine medical visits where substance use is discussed but not specifically categorized. The code is frequently used in clinical settings as a placeholder diagnosis when more specific substance information isn't yet available.",
