    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that someone has a history of using various psychoactive drugs or substances (not limited to a single type), but they are currently in remission—meaning they are no longer actively using and have stopped the behavior. The person may have struggled with multiple types of drugs or alcohol, and this code documents that their substance use disorder is being managed and they've achieved a period of recovery or abstinence.",
    "whoUses": "This code is used by addiction medicine specialists, psychiatrists, primary care doctors, and mental health counselors when documenting a patient's recovery status from substance use disorders. It commonly appears on EOB statements for patients in substance abuse treatment programs, counseling sessions, or ongoing recovery monitoring, and is often used to track long-term outcomes in addiction care.",
