    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a situation where someone has used an unspecified psychoactive drug (a substance that affects the brain and behavior) and is experiencing delirium—a serious mental state marked by confusion, hallucinations, rapid mood changes, and difficulty thinking clearly. Delirium from drug intoxication is a medical emergency because the person may be disoriented, unable to recognize people or places, and at risk of harming themselves or others. This condition requires immediate medical attention to identify which substance was used and provide appropriate treatment.",
    "whoUses": "Emergency medicine physicians, psychiatrists, toxicologists, and hospital medicine doctors use this code when treating patients presenting with acute drug intoxication and altered mental status. It commonly appears in hospital admissions and emergency department records but is less frequently seen on standard patient EOBs since it typically reflects acute inpatient or emergency care episodes.",
