    "shortDesc": "Oth psychoactive substance use, unsp with intoxication, unsp",
    "longDesc": "Other psychoactive substance use, unspecified with intoxication, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a situation where someone is experiencing intoxication (being under the influence) from a psychoactive substance—like drugs or inhalants—but the specific substance causing the intoxication is not documented or known. Intoxication means the substance is actively affecting the person's mind and body, causing impaired thinking, coordination, or behavior at the time of the medical visit.",
    "whoUses": "Addiction medicine specialists, emergency department physicians, psychiatrists, and substance abuse counselors use this code when treating patients who present with signs of intoxication but either cannot identify the specific drug used or have taken multiple substances. This code is more commonly seen in hospital records and emergency department documentation than on routine patient EOBs, though it may appear if the visit involved substance-related treatment or evaluation.",
