    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a serious condition where someone has been using various psychoactive substances (drugs or alcohol) and is now experiencing delirium—severe confusion, hallucinations, and disorientation—as their body goes through withdrawal. Withdrawal delirium is a medical emergency that occurs when the substance is suddenly stopped or reduced, and the person may be agitated, disoriented, or unable to recognize their surroundings. This condition requires immediate medical attention because it can be life-threatening.",
