    "longDesc": "Cyclothymic disorder",
    "plainEnglish": "Cyclothymic disorder is a mood condition where you experience repeated cycles of mild depression and mild elevation of mood (hypomania) that last for years, but are less severe than bipolar disorder. Your mood swings are noticeable enough to interfere with your daily life, relationships, or work, but you don't have the extreme highs and lows that characterize full bipolar disorder. Most people with this condition feel like they're on an emotional rollercoaster, alternating between periods of low energy and sadness with periods of increased creativity, confidence, and activity.",
