    "plainEnglish": "Fear of thunderstorms is an intense, overwhelming anxiety that occurs when someone expects or experiences a thunderstorm. People with this fear may experience panic symptoms like rapid heartbeat, sweating, or an urgent need to hide or escape when they hear thunder or see lightning, even though they understand intellectually that the risk is minimal. This phobia can significantly disrupt daily life during storm season or make it difficult to be outdoors or travel when storms are possible.",
