    "shortDesc": "Post-traumatic stress disorder, chronic",
    "longDesc": "Post-traumatic stress disorder, chronic",
    "plainEnglish": "Post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) is a mental health condition that develops after experiencing or witnessing a traumatic event—such as violence, serious injury, accident, or other life-threatening situations. When PTSD is chronic, it means the symptoms have persisted for more than three months and continue to significantly affect your daily life, including intrusive memories or flashbacks, avoidance of reminders, negative mood changes, and heightened anxiety or startle responses. This ongoing condition requires ongoing mental health treatment to help you process the trauma and manage symptoms.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, psychologists, licensed therapists, and primary care physicians diagnose and treat chronic PTSD. This code commonly appears on patient EOB statements when individuals receive counseling, therapy, psychiatric medication management, or inpatient mental health treatment related to long-standing trauma symptoms.",
