    "plainEnglish": "Hypochondriacal disorder means you have persistent and excessive worry about having a serious illness, even though medical tests show you're physically healthy. This condition causes real anxiety and distress—you may frequently check your body for symptoms, seek repeated medical appointments, or misinterpret normal bodily sensations as signs of disease. The worry is difficult to control and significantly impacts your daily life, relationships, and overall well-being.",
