    "plainEnglish": "Hypochondriasis is a mental health condition where someone becomes excessively preoccupied with the idea that they have a serious illness, even though medical tests and doctor visits consistently show nothing is physically wrong. People with this condition often interpret normal body sensations (like a slight ache or fatigue) as signs of a major disease, leading to frequent doctor visits, health anxiety, and significant distress in their daily life.",
