    "plainEnglish": "Body dysmorphic disorder is a mental health condition where you become intensely preoccupied with perceived flaws in your appearance that are either minor or not observable to others. People with this condition often spend excessive time mirror-checking, grooming, or seeking reassurance about how they look, and this preoccupation causes significant distress or interferes with daily functioning, work, or relationships. The condition is driven by anxiety and can lead to avoidance of social situations or repeated cosmetic procedures in an attempt to fix imagined defects.",
