    "longDesc": "Depersonalization-derealization syndrome",
    "plainEnglish": "Depersonalization-derealization syndrome is a condition where you feel disconnected from your own body or surroundings, as if you're observing yourself from outside your body or watching the world through a fog. People with this condition experience a persistent sense of unreality or detachment, even though they know intellectually that what they're experiencing isn't actually happening. This typically occurs in response to severe stress, anxiety, or trauma, and can be very distressing, though it doesn't mean you're losing touch with reality.",
