    "code": "F51.04",
    "rawCode": "F5104",
    "shortDesc": "Psychophysiologic insomnia",
    "longDesc": "Psychophysiologic insomnia",
    "plainEnglish": "Psychophysiologic insomnia is a sleep disorder where your mind and body become trapped in a cycle of anxiety about sleep itself. You may worry so much about not sleeping that the stress and worry actually keep you awake, creating a pattern where fear of insomnia becomes the main obstacle to falling asleep. This is different from insomnia caused by a medical condition or sleep apnea—it's driven primarily by psychological and physical tension related to your relationship with sleep.",
    "whoUses": "Sleep medicine specialists, psychiatrists, and primary care physicians commonly diagnose and treat this condition. It frequently appears on EOB statements as it's a recognized diagnosis code used for billing sleep studies, behavioral sleep medicine consultations, and cognitive-behavioral therapy for insomnia (CBT-I).",
