    "longDesc": "Sleepwalking [somnambulism]",
    "plainEnglish": "Sleepwalking is a sleep disorder where you get up and walk around while you're still asleep, often without any awareness or memory of what you did. During these episodes, your brain is partially awake enough to control your muscles and movement, but not awake enough for you to be conscious or remember the event. People who sleepwalk may perform routine activities, leave their bed, or even leave their home while in this state.",
