    "shortDesc": "Puerperal psychosis",
    "longDesc": "Puerperal psychosis",
    "plainEnglish": "Puerperal psychosis is a severe mental health condition that develops in women shortly after giving birth, typically within the first few weeks postpartum. This condition involves a break from reality, which may include hallucinations, delusions, severe mood changes, or disorganized thinking—far more serious than postpartum depression or baby blues. While relatively rare (occurring in 1-2 births per 1,000), it is a psychiatric emergency that requires immediate hospitalization and treatment.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, perinatal psychiatrists, and obstetric care providers use this code to identify postpartum psychosis in new mothers. It appears on EOB statements when a patient receives inpatient psychiatric treatment or emergency psychiatric care following delivery, and may also appear when ongoing outpatient psychiatric management of this condition is documented.",
