    "longDesc": "Abuse of antacids",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes a pattern of misusing antacids—the medications people take to relieve heartburn and acid reflux—in a way that's harmful to your health. When someone repeatedly takes antacids in excessive amounts or more often than recommended, it can lead to serious problems like electrolyte imbalances, kidney damage, or other complications. This diagnosis is used when a healthcare provider identifies that antacid use has become problematic and is causing actual health damage rather than just providing relief.",
