    "plainEnglish": "Laxative abuse means you're using laxatives (medicines that help you have bowel movements) in a way that's harmful to your health—either taking them too often, in excessive amounts, or without medical supervision. This can happen because someone is trying to lose weight, dealing with constipation that won't go away, or struggling with an eating disorder, and it can lead to dehydration, electrolyte imbalances, and damage to your digestive system.",
