    "longDesc": "Abuse of other non-psychoactive substances",
    "plainEnglish": "This code describes the misuse or abuse of substances that don't affect the mind or mood, such as certain medications, herbal products, vitamins, or other non-addictive substances taken in harmful ways. A person might be repeatedly using these substances in ways they weren't intended—like taking excessive amounts of laxatives, enemas, or dietary supplements—causing physical or psychological problems. The key difference from other substance abuse is that these particular substances don't create the typical \"high\" or intoxication that drugs like alcohol or opioids do.",
