    "plainEnglish": "Schizoid personality disorder is a mental health condition where someone tends to be emotionally detached, prefers being alone, and has little interest in close relationships or social activities—even though they're able to function in daily life. People with this disorder often seem indifferent to praise or criticism and may have a rich inner life or interests (like hobbies or intellectual pursuits) that they focus on instead of connecting with others. It's different from schizophrenia; someone with schizoid personality disorder doesn't experience hallucinations or delusions, but rather a consistent pattern of social withdrawal and emotional distance.",
