    "plainEnglish": "Avoidant personality disorder is a long-standing pattern of behavior where you persistently avoid social situations, relationships, and activities due to intense fear of rejection, criticism, or embarrassment. People with this condition often feel inadequate or inferior, worry excessively about how others perceive them, and tend to isolate themselves even though they actually desire connection—this creates a painful cycle where the avoidance reinforces their anxiety rather than relieving it.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, psychologists, and mental health counselors use this code when diagnosing personality disorders in clinical and therapeutic settings. This code appears on EOBs less frequently than acute mental health diagnoses, but is commonly documented for patients engaged in long-term psychotherapy or psychiatric treatment.",
