    "shortDesc": "Dependent personality disorder",
    "longDesc": "Dependent personality disorder",
    "plainEnglish": "Dependent personality disorder is a mental health condition where someone has an excessive need to be taken care of by others and struggles to make decisions or take actions on their own. People with this condition often fear abandonment, have difficulty being alone, and may allow others to make important life decisions for them—such as where to live, what job to take, or how to spend money. They typically seek reassurance constantly and may feel helpless or anxious when they're not in a dependent relationship.",
