    "shortDesc": "Gender identity disorder of childhood",
    "longDesc": "Gender identity disorder of childhood",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis refers to a condition in children where there is a persistent and strong identification with a gender different from the sex assigned at birth, causing significant distress or impairment in daily functioning. The child may consistently express a desire to be the other gender, prefer clothing and activities typically associated with another gender, and experience emotional or social difficulties related to this gender incongruence. This is different from occasional gender non-conformity and represents a persistent pattern that affects the child's wellbeing.",
    "whoUses": "Pediatric psychiatrists, child psychologists, and pediatricians use this code when evaluating and treating children with persistent gender dysphoria. This code is less commonly seen on patient EOBs compared to adult mental health diagnoses, as it is typically used in specialized mental health or developmental pediatric settings.",
