    "code": "F68.10",
    "rawCode": "F6810",
    "shortDesc": "Factitious disorder imposed on self, unspecified",
    "longDesc": "Factitious disorder imposed on self, unspecified",
    "plainEnglish": "Factitious disorder imposed on self means you are deliberately producing, exaggerating, or faking symptoms or signs of illness in yourself in order to gain attention, sympathy, or to assume the sick role—without an external reward like money or avoiding work. This is different from malingering (faking for obvious external benefit) because the primary motivation is psychological rather than material. People with this condition may fabricate medical histories, tamper with medical tests, or actually harm themselves to create the appearance of illness.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, psychologists, and behavioral health specialists use this code when evaluating patients with suspected factitious disorder. It may also be used by primary care physicians, internists, or emergency room doctors who have ruled out genuine medical conditions and identified a pattern of intentional symptom production. This code rarely appears on patient EOB statements as a primary diagnosis because patients with factitious disorder typically do not seek mental health treatment voluntarily.",
