    "code": "F68.A",
    "rawCode": "F68A",
    "shortDesc": "Factitious disorder imposed on another",
    "longDesc": "Factitious disorder imposed on another",
    "plainEnglish": "This diagnosis describes a situation where someone deliberately causes, exaggerates, or fabricates illness symptoms or medical problems in another person—typically someone dependent on them, like a child or elderly relative—in order to gain attention, sympathy, or other psychological benefits for themselves. This is a serious form of abuse and deception that can lead to unnecessary medical treatments, hospitalizations, and harm to the victim. The person doing this knows they are creating the false illness but continues the behavior anyway.",
    "whoUses": "Mental health professionals, psychiatrists, social workers, child protective services, and hospital-based abuse teams use this code when they identify cases of intentional harm through medical deception. It commonly appears in pediatric, geriatric, and psychiatric settings, and while it may appear on EOBs, it's more typically used in medical records, legal documentation, and abuse investigation reports rather than on routine patient billing statements.",
