    "code": "F68.8",
    "rawCode": "F688",
    "shortDesc": "Other specified disorders of adult personality and behavior",
    "longDesc": "Other specified disorders of adult personality and behavior",
    "plainEnglish": "This code is used when a patient has a personality or behavioral disorder that doesn't fit neatly into other specific categories—it's a catch-all diagnosis for unusual patterns of thinking, feeling, or acting that cause problems in daily life or relationships. The condition is significant enough that a healthcare provider felt it needed to be documented and treated, but it doesn't match the criteria for disorders like narcissistic personality disorder, borderings personality disorder, or other well-defined conditions. Patients might experience ongoing struggles with how they relate to others, manage stress, or regulate their emotions.",
    "whoUses": "Mental health specialists, psychiatrists, and psychologists commonly use this code in outpatient mental health clinics, therapy practices, and psychiatric hospitals. It appears on EOB statements when insurance processes claims for mental health evaluations, therapy sessions, or psychiatric consultations for personality or behavioral concerns.",
