    "shortDesc": "Unspecified disorder of adult personality and behavior",
    "longDesc": "Unspecified disorder of adult personality and behavior",
    "plainEnglish": "This code is used when a doctor has identified that you have some kind of personality or behavioral problem as an adult, but they haven't yet determined the specific diagnosis or condition causing it. It might appear on your paperwork when your doctor is still evaluating your symptoms or behavior and needs more time or testing to pinpoint exactly what's going on. Think of it as a temporary placeholder diagnosis while your healthcare team gathers more information.",
    "whoUses": "Psychiatrists, psychologists, primary care physicians, and behavioral health specialists use this code during initial evaluations or when the specific personality or behavioral disorder hasn't been clearly identified. It commonly appears on patient EOBs and medical records as a preliminary diagnosis code, often replaced with a more specific diagnosis after further assessment.",
