    "code": "F70",
    "rawCode": "F70",
    "shortDesc": "Mild intellectual disabilities",
    "longDesc": "Mild intellectual disabilities",
    "plainEnglish": "Mild intellectual disability means a person has significant limitations in thinking, reasoning, and learning abilities that began during childhood development. People with this condition typically have an IQ between 50-69 and may need some support with complex tasks like managing finances or learning new job skills, but many can live independently, work, and maintain relationships with appropriate help and accommodations.",
    "whoUses": "Pediatricians, developmental medicine specialists, psychologists, psychiatrists, and special education professionals use this code during initial evaluations and ongoing care. It commonly appears on EOB statements for children and young adults receiving developmental evaluations, school-based services, or disability-related healthcare.",
