    "code": "F71",
    "rawCode": "F71",
    "shortDesc": "Moderate intellectual disabilities",
    "longDesc": "Moderate intellectual disabilities",
    "plainEnglish": "Moderate intellectual disability means a person has significant limitations in thinking, reasoning, and learning skills that affect their ability to function independently in daily life. Someone with this level of disability typically needs ongoing support with tasks like self-care, communication, work, and managing money or health decisions, though they may be able to learn practical skills and live semi-independently with assistance.",
    "whoUses": "This code is used by psychiatrists, developmental pediatricians, clinical psychologists, special education specialists, and disability services providers when documenting cognitive assessment results and treatment planning for individuals with developmental disabilities. It commonly appears on EOB statements for mental health services, special education evaluations, vocational rehabilitation, and disability benefits documentation.",
