    "longDesc": "Profound intellectual disabilities",
    "plainEnglish": "Profound intellectual disabilities means a person has severe limitations in thinking, learning, and reasoning abilities that significantly impact their daily functioning and independence. People with this condition typically have an IQ below 20 and require extensive support for basic activities like eating, hygiene, communication, and self-care throughout their lifetime.",
    "whoUses": "Developmental pediatricians, psychiatrists, neurologists, and special education specialists use this code when diagnosing and managing severe intellectual disabilities. It commonly appears on EOB statements for individuals receiving long-term developmental services, residential care coordination, or specialized medical support.",
