    "shortDesc": "SYNGAP1-related intellectual disability",
    "longDesc": "SYNGAP1-related intellectual disability",
    "plainEnglish": "SYNGAP1-related intellectual disability is a rare genetic condition caused by mutations in the SYNGAP1 gene, which affects how the brain develops and functions. People with this condition have intellectual and developmental delays that are present from early childhood, and they may also experience seizures, autism spectrum behaviors, and difficulty with speech and movement. The severity can vary widely, ranging from mild learning difficulties to more significant developmental challenges that require ongoing support.",
    "whoUses": "Geneticists, developmental pediatricians, neurologists, and psychiatrists use this code when evaluating children with developmental delays and suspected genetic causes, particularly those with a positive genetic test for SYNGAP1 mutations. This code appears less frequently on patient EOB statements since it requires genetic confirmation and is typically documented in specialty clinics rather than routine primary care visits.",
