    "plainEnglish": "This code describes intellectual disability (difficulty with thinking, learning, and reasoning) that is caused by a genetic condition not listed elsewhere in the classification system. Your genes naturally control how your brain develops and functions, and sometimes genetic variations can affect how your brain processes information and adapts to new situations. People with this condition typically have below-average intellectual functioning that shows up during childhood or early adulthood and may need varying levels of support with daily life skills and learning.",
    "whoUses": "Developmental pediatricians, child neurologists, geneticists, and psychiatrists use this code when evaluating children with suspected genetic causes of intellectual disability. It appears on EOB statements when genetic testing or specialized neurodevelopmental evaluation has been performed to identify the underlying cause of intellectual disability, though it's more commonly used in clinical documentation than on routine patient billing statements.",
