    "shortDesc": "Unspecified intellectual disabilities",
    "longDesc": "Unspecified intellectual disabilities",
    "plainEnglish": "This code indicates that a person has an intellectual disability—meaning they have significant limitations in how well they can learn, reason, and adapt to everyday situations—but the doctor hasn't specified exactly what type or cause it is. Intellectual disabilities affect a person's ability to understand complex concepts, manage self-care, communicate, and live independently, and they typically begin before adulthood. This is a catch-all code used when the specific type of intellectual disability (like Down syndrome or autism-related intellectual disability) hasn't been identified or documented yet.",
    "whoUses": "Developmental pediatricians, neurologists, psychiatrists, and special education professionals use this code when evaluating someone with intellectual disability. It commonly appears on EOBs for evaluations, testing, therapy services, and ongoing management of intellectual disabilities, particularly when a more specific diagnosis hasn't yet been determined.",
