    "longDesc": "Transient tic disorder",
    "plainEnglish": "A transient tic disorder is a condition where a person experiences involuntary, repetitive movements or sounds (called tics) that last for a short period of time, typically a few weeks to a few months. These tics—such as eye blinking, shoulder shrugging, or throat clearing—happen automatically without the person meaning to do them and can be temporarily suppressed with effort, though doing so usually creates tension. The tics are not caused by medications or other medical conditions, and they resolve on their own without long-term treatment.",
